WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.425
Where do connectors go?

2
00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:04.185
They're outbound only,
with no inbound ports,

3
00:00:04.185 --> 00:00:08.786
they run on the program's server standard
of Windows Server 2019 or later,

4
00:00:08.786 --> 00:00:11.009
and they come at least two to a group,

5
00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:14.613
so a patch or an outage doesn't
take the applications down.

6
00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:15.801
Now the clouds.

7
00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:20.911
Learn describes Private Access as reaching
private apps across hybrid and multicloud

8
00:00:20.911 --> 00:00:23.572
environments, through
connectors on Windows

9
00:00:23.572 --> 00:00:26.513
Server hosts with line of
sight to the application.

10
00:00:26.513 --> 00:00:31.587
So an application in A W S, Google Cloud,
or Oracle Cloud Infrastructure gets

11
00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:36.662
a connector group in that cloud's network,
exactly as an on-premises one does.

12
00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:41.189
But Learn has no connector procedure
specific to any of those three clouds,

13
00:00:41.189 --> 00:00:43.524
so the guide marks it not yet specified,

14
00:00:43.524 --> 00:00:47.160
and it doesn't compare those
providers' own access services.
